<%# One thing being judged, framed so the evidence and the verdict are on screen
    together (see review_card.css). Render with `render layout:` — the block is the
    body, and i18n inside it must use ABSOLUTE keys.

    `actions` is pre-rendered markup rather than a second block because the bar sits
    OUTSIDE the scrolling body. Leave `source` out and pass `source_attrs` instead
    when the evidence exists only in the browser — a capture's poster is never
    uploaded, so the client writes it into the pane itself. %>
<%# locals: (id:, actions:, source: nil, frame_class: nil, frame_attrs: {}, source_attrs: {}) %>
<%= tag.div id: id, class: ["review-card", frame_class], **frame_attrs do %>
  <%= tag.div source, class: "review-card__source", **source_attrs %>
  <div class="review-card__body"><%= yield %></div>
  <%= actions %>
<% end %>
